---
Restore an instance from a `.tensor-wasm` archive via the API

Usage: tensor-wasm snapshot restore [OPTIONS] --input <INPUT> --as-instance <AS_INSTANCE> --server <SERVER>

Options:
      --input <INPUT>
          Path to the `.tensor-wasm` archive to upload
      --tenant <TENANT>
          Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests via `X-TensorWasm-Tenant`. Zero (the default) suppresses the header for backwards compatibility [default: 0]
      --as-instance <AS_INSTANCE>
          Identifier to assign to the restored instance
      --server <SERVER>
          Base URL of the target TensorWasm server (e.g. `http://localhost:8080`)
      --max-decompressed <MAX_DECOMPRESSED>
          Maximum decompressed snapshot size we'll accept, in bytes. Mirrors the server-side cap so the CLI rejects oversized archives without a pointless upload [default: 268435456]
      --hmac-key-file <PATH>
          Path to a 32-byte HMAC-SHA256 key. The file is interpreted as 64 hex characters if it's that length (whitespace trimmed), otherwise as 32 raw bytes. Mismatched length → error
      --require-signature
          Refuse to restore an unsigned (v2) snapshot
  -h, --help
          Print help
